{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SCOPING NOTE. This epic's attestation went stale-head the moment the first child's commit landed (signed at b872bc3c8, HEAD e78c86be1). Cause: it was UNSCOPED — an epic with no file_impact dies on EVERY commit, which is the documented stale-head mode and would have recurred on every single child change through to the close. Setting file_impact now costs nothing because the attestation was ALREADY dead, and it makes the eventual close-time review durable: a scoped attestation only goes stale-code when one of ITS OWN dependency files drifts. The paths are the union of the four children's declared impacts. Sequencing that matters and burned a cycle earlier on this epic: do NOT edit this while a review of THIS ticket is in flight, and do not edit a CHILD's material while a review of this parent is in flight — that is what produced the stale-pin-drift that blocked the first sign attempt."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785568660498637001,"uuid":"dc91356c-e46a-41c3-a050-ce2b76656305"}